  "description": "NaCuO crystallizes in the tetragonal I4/mmm space group. Na¹⁺ is bonded in a see-saw-like geometry to four equivalent O²⁻ atoms. There are two shorter (2.33 Å) and two longer (2.34 Å) Na-O bond lengths. Cu¹⁺ is bonded in a linear geometry to two equivalent O²⁻ atoms. Both Cu-O bond lengths are 1.83 Å. O²⁻ is bonded to four equivalent Na¹⁺ and two equivalent Cu¹⁺ atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing ONa₄Cu₂ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 1-14°.",
